add('electron-ohos-arkts-call-bridge','Call ArkTS from an Electron addon through a bound adapter','native-addon',['electron'],
 'Reach OS capabilities that Electron does not expose through an adapter library linked to the runtime and an ArkTS function binding, with a bounded wait on asynchronous replies.',
 'Electron JavaScript needs a capability such as a device identifier or screen capture, which only ArkTS or a system kit provides, and an ordinary Node addon cannot reach the ArkTS VM.',
 'Electron OH hosts where you control both the ArkTS host and a native addon. Reviewed sources build against a runtime tree and link libelectron.so and an AKI binding library. The ArkTS registration side was not in the reviewed repository, and no runtime version compatibility was established. Some runtimes are documented by the source as offering systemPreferences.callArkTSFunction, which should be checked first.',
 'ArkTS bridge|AKI|JSBind|GetJSFunction|node-addon-api|AsyncWorker|callArkTSFunction|libaki_jsbind|Electron addon',
 ['electron-ohos-napi-symbol-owner','electron-ohos-native-addon-abi','napi-thread-and-handle-lifetime'],
 ['Check whether your runtime provides a direct API, and use that if it does, as a custom binding has more to maintain.',
  'On the ArkTS host, register named functions with the binding library before the Electron main script needs them.',
  'Build an adapter shared library that links the binding library and libelectron.so, and look functions up with aki::JSBind::GetJSFunction, checking for null.',
  'Wrap the adapter with a node-addon-api .node. Run asynchronous calls in a Napi::AsyncWorker that waits on a condition variable with a timeout, so the Electron main thread is never blocked by a missing reply.',
  'Return a structured reply such as JSON {code, data, msg}, and map timeouts and missing functions to explicit errors.'],
 'The reviewed waits are 15 s, with 10 s for capture. Avoid single global promise slots like the reviewed authorization path, which are unsafe for concurrent calls. Rebuild the adapter whenever the runtime or its ABI changes.',
 'Calling a VM value from the wrong environment. Waiting with no timeout. Assuming the ArkTS function exists at startup. Linking the addon against a different runtime build than the one that ships.',
 'Invoke each function synchronously and asynchronously, including with a missing registration, a thrown ArkTS error and a slow handler. Run concurrent calls and repeat after a window reload.',
 [('electron-ohos-bridge',B+'ets_bridge_adapter.cc'),('electron-ohos-bridge',B+'CMakeLists.txt'),('electron-ohos-bridge','ets_bridge_addon/bridge_worker.h')],
 limitations=['Source files carry all-rights-reserved headers, so provenance retains hashes and locations only, and the guidance describes API use in general terms.'])
add('ohos-input-injection-authorization','Request authorization before injecting OS input events on OH','input',[],
 'Call OH_Input_RequestInjection and wait for its callback before OH_Input_InjectMouseEvent or OH_Input_InjectKeyEvent, and stamp events with monotonic time so click detection works.',
 'Simulated mouse or keyboard events are rejected, or injected double-clicks register as separate single clicks.',
 'Native apps using the OH input NDK (ohinput) for automation or remote control. A user authorization prompt appears; the reviewed code does not show a permission declaration, so check the current API docs and product policy. Coordinates assume display 0 in the reviewed code, which does not fit multi-monitor PCs.',
 'OH_Input_RequestInjection|OH_Input_InjectMouseEvent|OH_Input_InjectKeyEvent|INPUT_INJECTION_AUTHORIZING|OH_Input_GetPointerLocation|double-click|input injection|remote control',
 ['arkweb-synthetic-input-exclusions','ohos-virtual-hid-device-injection','electron-ohos-arkts-call-bridge'],
 ['Call OH_Input_RequestInjection with a callback. Treat INPUT_SUCCESS and INPUT_INJECTION_AUTHORIZING as pending until the callback delivers a status, INPUT_INJECTION_AUTHORIZED as granted, and anything else as an error.',
  'Wait with a timeout long enough for a person to respond (60 s in the reviewed code) and report a denial to the caller.',
  'Create events with OH_Input_CreateMouseEvent or OH_Input_CreateKeyEvent, and set action, button or key, and position.',
  'Set action time from CLOCK_MONOTONIC in microseconds. The source comment says this makes double-clicks recognizable.',
  'Choose the display explicitly with OH_Input_SetMouseEventDisplayId, using the display from OH_Input_GetPointerLocation or your mapping rather than a constant. Destroy each event after injection.'],
 'Injection acts on the whole system, so tie it to an explicit user action. A virtual HID device is the alternative for hardware-like input.',
 'Injecting while authorization is pending. Using a wall clock. Hard-coding display 0. Keeping one global promise so overlapping requests overwrite each other.',
 'Test first-use grant, denial and timeout. Then inject single and double clicks, drags and key combinations across two displays, and check the target receives them in another window.',
 [('electron-ohos-bridge',B+'ets_bridge_adapter.cc')],limitations=['Hash-only evidence; source bytes not retained because of all-rights-reserved headers.'])
add('ohos-usb-driver-extension-binding','Claim a vendor USB device through an OH driver extension','peripheral',[],
 'Declare a driver extension matched by bus, vid and pid, bind it from the UI with deviceManager and talk to it over RPC, then claim the interface in native USB DDK code.',
 'A normal ability cannot claim or read a vendor USB device such as a pen tablet, and needs a driver-level path on a PC.',
 'HarmonyOS 2in1 apps using the Driver Development Kit. Requires ACCESS_DDK_USB, ACCESS_EXTENSIONAL_DEVICE_DRIVER and for HID ACCESS_DDK_HID, which may need special approval for your distribution channel; check before designing around it. Sample-level evidence with one device.',
 'driver extension|extensionAbilities driver|ACCESS_DDK_USB|deviceManager.queryDevices|bindDeviceDriver|OH_Usb_ClaimInterface|OH_Usb_SendPipeRequest|USB DDK|vid pid',
 ['ohos-virtual-hid-device-injection','ohos-usbfs-preload-compat','privileged-capability-gating'],
 ['In module.json5 declare an extensionAbilities entry of type driver with metadata for bus USB, vid and pid, and request the DDK permissions.',
  'In the UI call deviceManager.queryDevices(BusType.USB), find the device, call bindDeviceDriver and keep the returned remote object. Re-bind in onRemoteDied.',
  'In the extension handle onRemoteMessageRequest and pass requests to native code. Set context.area before using preferences if the driver can run before user unlock, as the sample sets EL1.',
  'In native code call OH_Usb_Init, OH_Usb_GetConfigDescriptor and OH_Usb_ClaimInterface, then use OH_Usb_CreateDeviceMemMap and OH_Usb_SendPipeRequest for transfers. Find the interface from the descriptor rather than hard-coding it.',
  'Release the interface and memory maps and finish the DDK on disconnect and unbind.'],
 'For a device already handled as standard HID or for simple control, usbManager with user authorization may be enough. An extension runs separately from the UI process, so design for RPC failure.',
 'Hard-coding the interface number from one device. Omitting re-bind after the extension dies. Assuming an app with the permission declared passes signing and store checks.',
 'Plug and unplug during use, kill the extension, sleep and resume, and connect a non-matching device. Confirm rebind works and no transfers leak.',
 [('pc-handwriting-pad','entry/src/main/module.json5'),('pc-handwriting-pad','entry/src/main/ets/driverability/driver.ts'),('pc-handwriting-pad','entry/src/main/ets/tool/RpcTool.ets'),('pc-handwriting-pad','entry/src/main/cpp/hello.cpp')])
