 'Create a virtual device with OH_Hid_CreateDevice declaring its properties and events, then send event batches ending in SYN_REPORT with OH_Hid_EmitEvent from a dedicated thread.',
 'Pen pressure or remapped keys read from a peripheral are not seen as system input by other applications.',
 'Driver-extension apps with ACCESS_DDK_HID on HarmonyOS 2in1, linking libhid.z.so. Sample-level evidence with a pen pad and keyboard; pressure behavior in target apps was not established.',
 'OH_Hid_CreateDevice|OH_Hid_EmitEvent|OH_Hid_DestroyDevice|HID_PROP_DIRECT|HID_ABS_PRESSURE|HID_BTN_TOOL_PEN|SYN_REPORT|pen pressure|virtual device',
 ['ohos-usb-driver-extension-binding','ohos-input-injection-authorization','device-gesture-capability'],
 ['Define a Hid_Device and Hid_EventProperties for each logical device: event types and key codes for a keyboard, and direct property, absolute axes and tool buttons for a pen pad.',
  'Set each axis minimum and maximum to match the hardware scale, including pressure, and scale incoming reports accordingly.',
  'Create devices with OH_Hid_CreateDevice and keep the returned ID, checking for failure.',
  'Queue events and emit on a dedicated thread: tool button, ABS_X, ABS_Y, ABS_PRESSURE, then the sync report closing the batch, so USB reads are not blocked by injection.',
  'Destroy devices with OH_Hid_DestroyDevice on disconnect and exit.'],
 'This registers a device, unlike event injection, which needs per-app authorization and has no hardware-like identity. Prefer standard HID where the system already handles the device.',
 'Omitting the sync report, so events are not applied. Using mismatched axis ranges. Leaving virtual devices behind after a crash or unplug.',
 'In a pressure-sensitive app, draw with varied pressure and eraser, remap keys, then unplug and replug. Confirm no duplicate device or stuck tool state remains.',
